WEBVTT

00:01:43.810 --> 00:01:45.310
Good morning!

00:01:45.310 --> 00:01:48.950
This is the front desk, 
with your wake-up call!

00:01:48.950 --> 00:01:50.060
Uh, right.

00:01:50.060 --> 00:01:52.680
Thanks, I'm awake.

00:01:52.680 --> 00:01:54.840
Have a nice day, Mister!

00:02:09.420 --> 00:02:10.650
Now, then...

00:02:27.730 --> 00:02:29.310
Time for work.

00:02:38.340 --> 00:02:40.100
I'm finally here...

00:02:42.630 --> 00:02:44.110
Center City.

00:02:57.540 --> 00:02:59.150
Good morning.

00:02:59.150 --> 00:02:59.970
Morning.

00:02:59.970 --> 00:03:01.890
How's the welcome party coming?

00:03:01.890 --> 00:03:04.410
We've already proceeded to phase two.

00:03:04.410 --> 00:03:06.180
There have been no oversights.

00:03:06.180 --> 00:03:07.680
We're up against the Ghost here.

00:03:07.680 --> 00:03:10.100
Make sure not to get yourself haunted.

00:03:10.100 --> 00:03:11.300
Right, Sir.

00:03:11.300 --> 00:03:16.790
Before the road repair erases the footprints,
I want to go check it out myself once again.

00:03:16.790 --> 00:03:19.090
We'll proceed with the 
steamroller plan right away.

00:03:19.090 --> 00:03:20.650
Now, don't be hasty.

00:03:21.730 --> 00:03:23.960
I have two or three things I'm curious about.

00:03:23.960 --> 00:03:27.470
Hold up the invitation until I've 
determined them one way or the other.

00:03:29.510 --> 00:03:30.060
Got it?

00:03:30.780 --> 00:03:33.310
Understood, Agent Hughes.

00:03:39.330 --> 00:03:41.800
I was asked out on a date!

00:03:41.800 --> 00:03:43.360
What do you think, Heroman?

00:03:43.620 --> 00:03:45.730
I'm kinda embarrassed.

00:03:47.410 --> 00:03:51.780
But, wait! The guy needs to 
take the lead on a date, right?

00:03:51.780 --> 00:03:54.960
I wonder where Lina would enjoy going to?

00:03:55.460 --> 00:03:57.930
What do you think, Heroman?

00:03:59.540 --> 00:04:02.610
<i>The barricade is set to be 
lifted at eight o'clock.</i>

00:04:02.610 --> 00:04:04.260
<i>#3 filming is complete.</i>

00:04:04.260 --> 00:04:05.720
<i>Proceeding to precision measurements.</i>

00:04:05.720 --> 00:04:09.720
<i>Nothing out of the ordinary detected 
in a 30 meter square perimeter.</i>

00:04:14.900 --> 00:04:17.550
This is where the trail cuts off.

00:04:28.430 --> 00:04:30.290
Onesy, twosy, threesy...

00:04:30.540 --> 00:04:35.770
I knew it... I'd better 
put in some work or else.

00:04:37.890 --> 00:04:40.320
Yes! Coming, coming!

00:04:41.090 --> 00:04:42.670
Who is...

00:04:50.540 --> 00:04:52.910
S-Sis?!

00:04:58.440 --> 00:04:59.540
Hey, you alien!

00:04:59.540 --> 00:05:01.220
Show your true form!

00:05:01.220 --> 00:05:03.690
Sis, it's me! Joey!

00:05:03.690 --> 00:05:05.460
What are you talkin' about?

00:05:05.460 --> 00:05:08.560
My little brother is a tiny munchkin!

00:05:08.560 --> 00:05:11.200
Well, I grew a bit in four years!

00:05:11.510 --> 00:05:13.590
It's Holly!

00:05:13.590 --> 00:05:15.460
Granny, I'm home.

00:05:16.230 --> 00:05:19.190
Don't worry. I caught the alien.

00:05:19.190 --> 00:05:21.210
I'm Joey!

00:05:24.280 --> 00:05:29.320
I thought you were touring with 
your band on the east coast?

00:05:29.590 --> 00:05:35.900
I heard that Center City was attacked by 
aliens so I came runnin' all the way here.

00:05:37.510 --> 00:05:39.640
It's been three months since then!

00:05:39.640 --> 00:05:43.120
I didn't have the money to 
get here so quick, sheesh.

00:05:43.120 --> 00:05:44.710
Here, it's a souvenir.

00:05:47.520 --> 00:05:48.610
You're old enough, right?

00:05:49.610 --> 00:05:50.900
I-I'm not...

00:05:50.900 --> 00:05:53.980
I wish you'd have at least called...

00:05:53.980 --> 00:05:56.870
Oh yeah, that would have been a good idea.

00:05:57.490 --> 00:05:58.700
She hasn't changed.

00:05:58.700 --> 00:06:00.970
Doing things at her own pace, as always.

00:06:00.970 --> 00:06:02.330
You say something?

00:06:02.330 --> 00:06:04.400
N-No, nothing.

00:06:04.400 --> 00:06:06.290
I'll make some coffee.

00:06:06.290 --> 00:06:08.010
Five lumps of sugar, please!

00:06:08.010 --> 00:06:11.880
I came running here, but what a letdown.

00:06:11.880 --> 00:06:14.460
There ain't any aliens around anymore.

00:06:15.090 --> 00:06:17.390
It happened three months ago!

00:06:17.390 --> 00:06:19.500
You're always like this, Sis...

00:06:19.500 --> 00:06:23.310
Egocentric and selfish... You never 
care at all about the people around you.

00:06:23.620 --> 00:06:26.820
Well, I came all this way so 
I ain't leavin' right away.

00:06:27.170 --> 00:06:29.420
I'll probably crash here two or three days.

00:06:37.700 --> 00:06:39.420
Damn, it's hot!

00:06:39.420 --> 00:06:41.770
This is why I hate the west coast!

00:06:41.770 --> 00:06:46.260
Dr. Minami. We have a request for a meeting.

00:06:47.060 --> 00:06:48.610
From who?

00:06:48.610 --> 00:06:50.890
They say they're someone with the government,

00:06:50.890 --> 00:06:54.260
but it seems they wish to tell 
you the details only in person.

00:06:54.260 --> 00:06:55.210
Accept it.

00:06:55.210 --> 00:06:56.420
Yes, sir.

00:06:56.420 --> 00:06:58.330
Finally they're here.

00:06:58.330 --> 00:07:00.710
It's been three months since we've 
been helping the reconstruction.

00:07:00.710 --> 00:07:02.770
What took them so long?

00:07:03.090 --> 00:07:04.530
These are gross!

00:07:04.530 --> 00:07:05.700
Give me another one!

00:07:09.320 --> 00:07:13.300
That's my favorite, limited time 
only, pumpkin flavored cereal!

00:07:13.300 --> 00:07:15.240
What do you care, I ain't eating that much!

00:07:15.510 --> 00:07:16.760
Yes, you are!

00:07:16.760 --> 00:07:19.860
Stop being such a nag. That ain't cool, Bro.

00:07:25.090 --> 00:07:27.090
I just got in the shower!

00:07:27.090 --> 00:07:29.190
I wanna clean off after the trip!

00:07:29.190 --> 00:07:31.530
You go after me. I'm first.

00:07:32.580 --> 00:07:34.700
How does that work exactly?

00:07:35.800 --> 00:07:37.470
Sis, why are you stripping?

00:07:37.810 --> 00:07:39.710
Let's just shower together, then.

00:07:39.710 --> 00:07:40.710
I'm leaving!

00:07:40.710 --> 00:07:42.660
I'm leaving right now, 
so keep your clothes on!

00:07:42.660 --> 00:07:46.160
What's the big deal? We used to 
do this all the time, remember?

00:07:46.670 --> 00:07:49.070
I'm in middle school now!

00:07:52.360 --> 00:07:53.980
When did you...

00:07:53.980 --> 00:07:55.800
T-That's...

00:07:55.800 --> 00:07:57.080
Sis!

00:08:00.430 --> 00:08:02.900
Knock before you enter, will ya?

00:08:02.900 --> 00:08:06.840
But yeah, I see you still 
treasure this thing.

00:08:06.840 --> 00:08:08.540
Stop it.

00:08:08.540 --> 00:08:11.080
Dad's helmet is mine.

00:08:11.080 --> 00:08:12.740
Don't go wearing it around!

00:08:12.740 --> 00:08:14.380
Hmph! You and your father complex.

00:08:14.380 --> 00:08:16.710
So, what is it now?

00:08:16.710 --> 00:08:19.310
Joey, you sleep in the living room.

00:08:20.810 --> 00:08:23.430
You plan on making a lady sleep on the sofa?

00:08:23.430 --> 00:08:25.690
This room is now mine.

00:08:27.150 --> 00:08:29.440
Y-You're joking, right?

00:08:29.440 --> 00:08:33.310
You're always, always taking my...

00:08:31.290 --> 00:08:32.930
What's this?

00:08:36.780 --> 00:08:39.900
No! Anything but that, please!

00:08:39.900 --> 00:08:42.700
Don't worry, I won't break it.

00:08:42.700 --> 00:08:47.490
Sis, do you remember how much of 
my stuff you've broken before?

00:08:47.490 --> 00:08:49.840
I didn't break 'em. They just broke.

00:08:50.360 --> 00:08:53.580
Man... Caring so much about 
a stupid toy at your age.

00:08:53.580 --> 00:08:54.720
You're pathetic.

00:08:55.410 --> 00:08:58.220
So, Joey, how old are you?

00:08:58.220 --> 00:09:00.850
Whatever!

00:09:00.850 --> 00:09:02.610
That thing looks pretty expensive.

00:09:02.610 --> 00:09:04.850
Think we could get some cash by selling it?

00:09:06.000 --> 00:09:07.970
Don't even joke about that!

00:09:08.710 --> 00:09:11.970
Heroman isn't a toy, or something to be sold.

00:09:11.970 --> 00:09:13.610
He's my friend!

00:09:19.290 --> 00:09:20.510
Your friend?

00:09:20.510 --> 00:09:22.350
Oh, I get it, he's your friend!

00:09:22.350 --> 00:09:24.550
You're a riot!

00:09:24.550 --> 00:09:27.100
Hey, Joey, wait!

00:09:27.100 --> 00:09:28.490
Where are you going?

00:09:28.490 --> 00:09:29.760
To Psy's place.

00:09:35.070 --> 00:09:36.200
Pardon me.

00:09:36.810 --> 00:09:38.820
This is the first time we've met.

00:09:38.820 --> 00:09:44.310
I am Agent Hughes from the National 
Intelligence Agency, abbreviated NIA.

00:09:44.820 --> 00:09:47.110
Nice to meet you, Dr. Minami.

00:09:47.830 --> 00:09:50.080
Nice to meet you as well.

00:09:50.080 --> 00:09:52.530
You're from the NIA?

00:09:52.530 --> 00:09:58.070
So what does the agency under direct 
control of the President want with me?

00:09:58.370 --> 00:10:02.060
If you want the MR-1 to be formally 
adopted into the military, then...

00:10:02.060 --> 00:10:04.330
I'm afraid it's something else.

00:10:05.210 --> 00:10:09.860
We'd like your advice on a certain 
case we're investigating.

00:10:09.860 --> 00:10:13.490
Or more precisely, to hear your opinion.

00:10:13.490 --> 00:10:14.850
My opinion?

00:10:14.850 --> 00:10:20.300
Yes. And I would like for you to 
cooperate with us on this matter.

00:10:20.300 --> 00:10:21.850
Cooperate?

00:10:21.850 --> 00:10:23.180
Why me?

00:10:23.460 --> 00:10:27.440
We are an agency that answers 
directly to the President.

00:10:27.440 --> 00:10:31.690
We have a very deep connection 
with your clients.

00:10:32.030 --> 00:10:34.070
If you think about your future...

00:10:34.860 --> 00:10:37.650
So you're saying this is for my own good?

00:10:37.650 --> 00:10:42.320
By the way, I will write 
all the reports myself.

00:10:42.960 --> 00:10:45.900
Oh, I see then.

00:10:45.900 --> 00:10:49.200
Then, if you'll allow me to ask a question.

00:10:49.200 --> 00:10:50.600
Is that okay?

00:10:50.600 --> 00:10:53.460
Sure. Ask whatever you'd like.

00:10:53.460 --> 00:10:55.850
At the request of the government,

00:10:55.850 --> 00:10:59.890
or rather you used your great 
power as one close to the military

00:10:59.890 --> 00:11:04.670
to join in and aid the government's 
reconstruction in a grand way.

00:11:04.670 --> 00:11:09.240
This was designed as a demonstration 
of your robot, correct?

00:11:09.240 --> 00:11:15.360
But if that was the point, there are more 
prominent places, like near the White House.

00:11:15.360 --> 00:11:17.440
What are you trying to say?

00:11:17.990 --> 00:11:20.240
Allow me to be frank.

00:11:20.940 --> 00:11:26.920
What are you doing here in Center City?

00:11:38.830 --> 00:11:41.670
What?!

00:11:42.810 --> 00:11:45.430
That nightmare has returned?

00:11:45.680 --> 00:11:46.390
Yeah...

00:11:46.390 --> 00:11:48.160
Just great...

00:11:48.160 --> 00:11:51.080
Guess I'd better steer clear 
of your house for a while.

00:11:51.080 --> 00:11:54.890
She's only been here half a 
day and I'm already worn out.

00:11:54.890 --> 00:11:56.730
It's a disaster, huh?

00:11:56.730 --> 00:11:59.090
And it's only just begun.

00:11:59.600 --> 00:12:01.360
Holly, huh?

00:12:02.130 --> 00:12:06.770
It's been four years since 
she suddenly left town.

00:12:08.630 --> 00:12:10.350
It's all coming back to me...

00:12:10.910 --> 00:12:15.540
That dark period in our youth...

00:12:19.380 --> 00:12:26.510
Always pickin' a fight, rude, strong as 
heck, buttin' in at the wrong time...

00:12:26.510 --> 00:12:30.100
Who're you callin' beautiful, 
elegant, and graceful?

00:12:34.300 --> 00:12:35.470
H-Holly!

00:12:35.470 --> 00:12:36.770
Long time no see...

00:12:37.510 --> 00:12:39.310
What's with the leg?

00:12:39.310 --> 00:12:41.520
N-Nothing much...

00:12:41.520 --> 00:12:42.370
I see.

00:12:42.370 --> 00:12:45.710
Anyway, I have a favor to ask you two.

00:12:47.260 --> 00:12:49.280
Will you do it for me?

00:12:49.280 --> 00:12:51.910
Do what?

00:12:54.400 --> 00:12:58.920
Well then, I will contact 
you again in a few days.

00:12:58.920 --> 00:13:00.760
I'll be waiting.

00:13:02.790 --> 00:13:04.520
Cunning bastard.

00:13:07.560 --> 00:13:10.480
How could I not be surprised!

00:13:10.480 --> 00:13:15.060
In just one night the entire 
pile of wreckage was cleaned up.

00:13:15.310 --> 00:13:16.820
Any clues?

00:13:16.820 --> 00:13:19.620
If there were I'd go and
thank to guy myself.

00:13:19.620 --> 00:13:21.110
Thank them?

00:13:21.110 --> 00:13:23.120
Well sure.

00:13:23.120 --> 00:13:26.210
Thanks to them our schedule and 
budget is looking much better.

00:13:26.210 --> 00:13:28.160
What's there to complain about?

00:13:28.750 --> 00:13:30.100
Here, too?

00:13:30.520 --> 00:13:33.580
Well, I'd like to get back to work, so...

00:13:34.410 --> 00:13:36.300
One final question.

00:13:36.300 --> 00:13:41.430
What kind of person do you 
think this individual is?

00:13:42.580 --> 00:13:44.300
An ally of justice!

00:13:44.550 --> 00:13:47.480
Everyone around here thinks so.

00:13:49.050 --> 00:13:51.410
Ally of justice...

00:13:54.280 --> 00:13:58.850
Sheesh... So you just wanted 
us to show you around town?

00:13:59.100 --> 00:14:03.230
You leave for a bit and
everything changes in this city.

00:14:03.570 --> 00:14:07.180
So then, where do you 
want us to show you, Sis?

00:14:07.180 --> 00:14:09.880
A place with a lot of people, if you can.

00:14:09.880 --> 00:14:13.280
And a place where it won't 
matter if I stick out a little.

00:14:13.840 --> 00:14:15.240
What's that supposed to mean?

00:14:15.490 --> 00:14:16.400
Shut it!

00:14:16.400 --> 00:14:18.440
Stop complainin' and find a place!

00:14:18.890 --> 00:14:20.080
I'm gonna fall!

00:14:22.620 --> 00:14:23.650
Any results?

00:14:23.650 --> 00:14:25.300
I ended up questioning people.

00:14:25.300 --> 00:14:27.010
But I didn't get any proof.

00:14:27.260 --> 00:14:29.300
Then, we should go one by one...

00:14:29.300 --> 00:14:30.620
Now, wait.

00:14:30.620 --> 00:14:32.260
There's one thing that's peaked my interest.

00:14:33.430 --> 00:14:35.700
It's still only in the realm of conjecture,

00:14:35.700 --> 00:14:39.020
but all the incidents of the Ghost
have the same characteristic.

00:14:39.270 --> 00:14:42.240
Did you think of something, Agent Hughes?

00:14:42.240 --> 00:14:46.280
Yeah. Just a bit of an 
opening act for the party.

00:14:50.440 --> 00:14:52.860
How long are we going to go on like this?

00:14:52.860 --> 00:14:55.180
Ask that to my sister...

00:14:55.450 --> 00:14:56.960
I've decided on here.

00:14:57.910 --> 00:15:00.580
I'll set off a big firework right here!

00:15:02.780 --> 00:15:05.370
Huh? An explosion?

00:15:08.380 --> 00:15:11.150
Excuse me, what happened?

00:15:11.150 --> 00:15:12.670
Some accident.

00:15:12.670 --> 00:15:14.790
Seems there are some people left behind...

00:15:14.790 --> 00:15:15.720
People?

00:15:16.260 --> 00:15:19.520
That giant sphere destroyed this building.

00:15:19.520 --> 00:15:22.980
The foundation isn't doing so well, so 
the rescue squads can't get to them.

00:15:23.250 --> 00:15:24.650
Oh, no!

00:15:25.670 --> 00:15:27.230
What're you going to do, Joey?

00:15:27.230 --> 00:15:30.990
You could probably use Heroman 
to save them, but today...

00:15:30.990 --> 00:15:33.450
What are you two standin' around for?

00:15:34.340 --> 00:15:35.490
It's nothing!

00:15:38.430 --> 00:15:42.600
Psy, I've been entrusted with a 
great duty to protect Center City.

00:15:42.600 --> 00:15:44.100
W-What?

00:15:45.250 --> 00:15:46.700
Hey, wait!

00:15:46.700 --> 00:15:49.760
I'll be back soon, so handle things here!

00:15:50.300 --> 00:15:52.550
Hey, Joey! Where are you going?

00:15:52.900 --> 00:15:54.160
Joey!

00:15:55.890 --> 00:15:57.040
Psy.

00:15:57.860 --> 00:15:59.060
Hold my stuff.

00:16:00.350 --> 00:16:01.490
Holly!

00:16:08.320 --> 00:16:10.300
The accident happened above here.

00:16:23.910 --> 00:16:25.790
Heroman...

00:16:26.710 --> 00:16:28.250
Engage!

00:16:31.560 --> 00:16:33.170
Where are the people that were left behind?

00:16:36.640 --> 00:16:39.350
I knew you'd appear.

00:16:39.910 --> 00:16:42.100
I've been searching for you a long time.

00:16:42.680 --> 00:16:46.480
We finally meet, Mr. Ghost.

00:16:47.390 --> 00:16:49.650
He's been searching for Heroman?

00:16:49.650 --> 00:16:52.710
I apologize for tricking 
you into coming here.

00:16:52.710 --> 00:16:56.320
But I didn't think I could 
meet you any other way.

00:16:56.680 --> 00:17:00.260
Don't worry, there are no people nearby.

00:17:00.260 --> 00:17:02.300
That means this is a trap!

00:17:02.300 --> 00:17:05.710
So the people being left behind was a lie?

00:17:06.020 --> 00:17:09.160
I have a lot of things I want to ask you.

00:17:09.160 --> 00:17:11.030
About your relationship with the Skrugg,

00:17:11.030 --> 00:17:15.540
and the large amount of volunteer 
work you've been doing lately.

00:17:15.540 --> 00:17:21.310
But first... May I ask you what you are?

00:17:24.320 --> 00:17:26.060
Silence, eh?

00:17:26.310 --> 00:17:29.050
Or perhaps you cannot speak?

00:17:29.050 --> 00:17:30.940
This is bad. I have to escape.

00:17:30.940 --> 00:17:35.690
Oh, pardon me. Let me introduce myself first.

00:17:35.690 --> 00:17:39.570
I am from the NIA, an agency that 
answers directly to the President...

00:17:39.820 --> 00:17:40.850
Heroman!

00:17:43.860 --> 00:17:46.870
Hey now, we're not done talking yet!

00:17:50.630 --> 00:17:52.580
Crap, crap, crap!

00:17:52.580 --> 00:17:54.380
I've got to do something!

00:17:57.090 --> 00:18:00.320
Man, I was finally going to show my stuff,

00:18:00.320 --> 00:18:02.890
and the main guest goes 
wandering off somewhere!

00:18:08.270 --> 00:18:10.230
Oh, no!

00:18:13.820 --> 00:18:14.440
That's it!

00:18:15.070 --> 00:18:19.450
Heroman... Attack!

00:18:26.840 --> 00:18:29.000
Taking a shortcut through the floor?

00:18:40.610 --> 00:18:42.530
Heroman, let's go.

00:18:42.850 --> 00:18:43.430
Wait!

00:18:49.110 --> 00:18:52.600
At least listen to my whole introduction.

00:18:53.700 --> 00:18:54.400
I am...

00:19:10.250 --> 00:19:11.820
What's all the smoke?

00:19:33.090 --> 00:19:34.350
Cool...

00:19:45.920 --> 00:19:47.580
Hey!

00:19:49.920 --> 00:19:51.410
Sorry, Sis!

00:19:54.400 --> 00:19:55.500
Sheesh.

00:19:55.500 --> 00:19:58.750
Don't go leaving your cute 
sister and wandering off!

00:19:58.750 --> 00:20:00.510
I-I'm sorry.

00:20:01.280 --> 00:20:02.630
Whatever.

00:20:05.190 --> 00:20:07.950
Let's hurry and get back so I can start!

00:20:08.230 --> 00:20:09.760
Start?

00:20:10.120 --> 00:20:11.100
What?

00:20:26.260 --> 00:20:36.540
Does the clear blue sky know?

00:20:37.440 --> 00:20:47.750
Does even the kind wind know?

00:20:47.750 --> 00:20:53.850
Right or left, going either 
way it's the same anyway.

00:20:53.850 --> 00:20:59.770
I don't got no map...

00:20:59.770 --> 00:21:05.450
But the sky'll point out, like sproutin'.

00:21:05.720 --> 00:21:10.990
If I stretch out my hand, I 
should be able to find it.

00:21:11.270 --> 00:21:16.460
I want to be able to bloom, 
like dandelion fluff.

00:21:16.750 --> 00:21:23.550
If I wander, I'll be able 
to find it, I'm sure...

00:21:23.820 --> 00:21:27.170
Gently...

00:21:27.460 --> 00:21:33.010
At the base of the rainbow.

00:21:38.360 --> 00:21:41.590
Holly's gotten really good!

00:21:51.070 --> 00:21:55.200
Amazing, Sis! You're sure to be 
a big star with a song like that!

00:21:55.200 --> 00:21:58.960
I'll work hard to save up money and 
see you perform on stage sometime!

00:21:59.540 --> 00:22:02.700
Where are you heading to 
next? The east coast again?

00:22:02.700 --> 00:22:05.260
No, I think I'll stay here for a while.

00:22:07.990 --> 00:22:11.470
There's something interesting in this town.

00:22:20.690 --> 00:22:24.090
<b>"Can you hear this voice?"</b>

00:22:24.090 --> 00:22:31.560
<b>I've been calling that, always, from deep within my heart.</b>

00:22:34.370 --> 00:22:45.460
<b>Would you, all alone, let another lonely one be next to you?</b>

00:22:45.460 --> 00:22:51.010
<b>Because together it's not lonely, it's twoly.</b>

00:22:51.010 --> 00:22:56.140
<b>See, you're not alone any longer.</b>

00:22:57.280 --> 00:22:59.990
<b>Just because there's no one next to me</b>

00:22:59.990 --> 00:23:02.540
<b>doesn't mean that I'm lonely!</b>

00:23:02.540 --> 00:23:07.740
<b>For someone to notice this pain</b>

00:23:07.740 --> 00:23:13.270
<b>that heart must have surely cried.</b>

00:23:13.270 --> 00:23:16.650
<b>Right now, we'll crush to bits</b>

00:23:16.650 --> 00:23:20.350
<b>the fortress of our limitless sadness!</b>

00:23:20.350 --> 00:23:24.050
<b>I'll take you with me!</b>

00:23:24.050 --> 00:23:27.730
<b>Got it? I'm running through at full power.</b>

00:23:27.730 --> 00:23:31.470
<b>To where you're waiting, left behind</b>

00:23:31.470 --> 00:23:34.640
<b>in the place of tears...</b>

00:23:35.950 --> 00:23:39.770
<b>I believe in you, with burning passion!</b>

00:23:39.770 --> 00:23:43.560
<b>Come to me!</b>

00:23:51.280 --> 00:23:53.310
On the next Heroman:

00:23:53.910 --> 00:23:57.490
Why? Why won't everyone leave us alone?

00:23:57.490 --> 00:23:58.840
Why?

00:23:59.360 --> 00:24:01.870
Lina wants to get closer to Joey,

00:24:01.870 --> 00:24:04.670
so she successfully asked Joey out on a date.

00:24:05.330 --> 00:24:11.500
However a new threat appears 
and gets in the way.

00:24:12.230 --> 00:24:16.030
Next time on Heroman #12: Stalkers.

00:24:16.030 --> 00:24:18.660
Heroman... Attack!
